{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 47, :comments ["<b>In a garment of wool or in a garment of linen.</b> Our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: wool garments do not contract impurity through nega'im except for the wool of a pure animal, but not the wool of an impure animal. If the garment was a mixture of the wool of an impure animal and the wool of a pure animal — if the majority is of a pure animal, it contracts impurity through nega'im; and if the majority is of an impure animal, it does not contract impurity through nega'im."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:14.863303157Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}